ired Comey  admitting that part of it was to ease  the pressure on him because of the  Russia investigation and now the former  director of the CIA is confirming yeah  there was communication between Trump  and Russia the idea of oh this is all  just completely overblown Republicans  had an opportunity at this hearing you  could even argue that they had a duty to  really question John Brennan in the  service of finding out more about  whether or not the president colluded  with a foreign adversary that's  something that should go beyond politics  but instead these Republicans waste time  with John Brennan playing silly  political games trying to use semantic  tricks on John Brennan trying to make  the investigation look frivolous sweep  everything under the rug Republicans  haven't even been responding with that  disapproval after we found out that  Trump asked the DNI and director of the  NSA to lie to the public and say there's  no evidence of collusion and former CIA  director Brennan also criticized Trump  for sort of blurting out this Israeli  Intel to Russians in the Oval Office  take a look at this other clip from  Brennan's hearing two protocols are one  is that such intelligence classified  intelligence is not shared with visiting  foreign ministers or local ambassadors  it's shared through intelligence  channels because it needs to be handled  the right way and it needs to make sure  that it is not exposed he didn't do that  if again if the press charges are  accurate secondly before sharing any  classified intelligence with foreign  partners it needs to go back to the  originating agency to make sure that the  language in it is not even just  providing a substance going to reveal  sources of methods and compromise the  future collection capability yeah so  what John Brennan is saying there is  your everyday run-of-the-mill spy  recruiting Russian ambassador should not  casually be told about information that  would presumably be handled with extreme  care